        "text": "Selected Answer: C. Setting a minimum number of Cloud Run instances ensures that there are always a few instances running, even when there is no traffic. While this would prevent cold starts, it doesn't directly address the traffic spike issue, where the number of active instances needs to scale to accommodate the load. During a traffic spike, if the maximum number of Cloud Run instances is not capped, Cloud Run will still spin up new instances to handle the increased load...."
