    "correctRationale": "The requirement is that available capacity never decreases during the deploy. maxUnavailable=0 guarantees zero VMs are allowed out of service at once; maxSurge=1 permits creating one temporary extra VM so the new version comes up before an old one is removed. The alternatives either allow a capacity dip (maxUnavailable=1), stand up a parallel MIG (overkill), or delete everything (guaranteed outage).",
